WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
 [Applause]

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:18.680
 Well, this is a five page introduction, but my son made sure that it's double

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.000
 spaced and the fun is 18.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.000
 [Laughter]

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:31.000
 So on behalf of the Bafna, Fennessur and Patel families, I would like to thank

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.850
 the Cleveland International Hall of Fame for this tremendous honor bestowed

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:37.000
 upon our father.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.210
 We call my father Kakuza. In our region of India, Kakuza is a respectful title

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:48.000
 for father's younger brother.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.040
 My father lived in a joint family and since my father is the youngest of three

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:58.000
 brothers, all my cousins, his brother's children, called him Kakuza.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:05.000
 As a result, I, my sister and my brother also called him Kakuza.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:11.260
 It is a common occurrence in our village and has continued here at Cleveland as

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:12.000
 well.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:17.880
 Kakuza was born to a middle class business family in a small village in

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.000
 Northwestern State of Rajasan, India.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:27.040
 Though I do not remember much about my grandfather, I do know that he was a

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:31.840
 simple man with an iron will, dear him to truth, honesty, compassion and

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:33.000
 service to others.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.720
 These values have been instilled in Kakuza and he passed them on to his

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:42.000
 children, grandchildren and great-granddaughter now.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:48.000
 By sixth grade, Kakuza decided that he wanted to pursue medicine.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:53.530
 Since our village only had a school till seventh grade, he had to be enrolled

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:58.000
 and moved to a neighboring village for further studies.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:05.290
 There in eighth grade, he shared an apartment with three boys. They cooked,

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:09.000
 cleaned, went to school and studied.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:16.150
 Imagine today sending an eighth grader away from home to live with three other

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:17.000
 boys.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:23.210
 Clearly, my grandfather had full confidence in him and Kakuza never let him

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:24.000
 down.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:36.360
 He married my mother Kambla when he was 18, was still in medical school and as

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:37.000
 the saying goes, behind every successful man, there is a woman.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.000
 Kakuza received unconditional love and support from my mother.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:48.000
 She was also a lady of strong will, compassion and of service to the community.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:54.290
 Equipped with scarcely a fifth grade education, for the sake of her family, she

00:02:54.290 --> 00:03:00.000
 reluctantly agreed to move to the US when she was 31 years old.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:07.240
 She struggled to learn English, to drive and learn ways of her new home. But

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:10.000
 she did this with a beautiful smile.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:16.460
 She taught us the meaning of love, respect, kindness, generosity and

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.000
 hospitality.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:23.000
 Kakuza decided to settle in the US, but he never forgot his roots.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:28.610
 Like his father, he lived a simple life. He continues to give back to his

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:35.000
 community in India and his adopted country by building schools and hospitals.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:41.160
 In recognition of his work, the people of his village in India presented him

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:49.000
 with their highest honor in front of nearly 10,000 in December of 2014.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:53.980
 He has been a pillar of the Indian community's equipment. He has never said no

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:58.000
 to anybody because he is a man of few words.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:03.000
 Yet he walks the walk by delivering his promises.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:08.000
 He is the kind of friend you want in your time of need.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:13.000
 He practiced medicine and bed for nearly 40 years.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:19.220
 He is loved by it, loved and admired by his colleagues, subordinates, and most

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:21.000
 of all, his patients.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:28.000
 Kakuza, I have not known a more loving and giving man than you.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:33.630
 You have gave an incredible path for your children, grandchildren and a great

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:35.000
 friend of mine.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:39.000
 We are proud of, proud and overjoyed as you receive this honor.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:43.000
 Thank you to all who made this evening possible.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:50.060
 And finally, a special thanks to our extended family in Cleveland and to my

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:55.000
 cousin and brother-in-law who came from India for this event.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:20.000
 [applause]

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.890
 I'm sorry to give you the microphone, but what a testament that people came

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.000
 from India number one.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:30.590
 And that for the first time ever, the Hall of Fame has a one-year-old in the

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:31.000
 end.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:34.000
 They wanted to bring to share this evening.

